"""Reference oracle + client I/O for the ${model} correctness gate (read-only).

This is the ONE model-specific file. The modality checker/benchmark call these
hooks; the model-specific request shape, response decode, and the reference
oracle live here. Copy to ``instances/${model}.reference.py`` and fill in.

Hooks (single client request — no walks, that is the port's internal detail):
- sample_input()               -> a fixed, deterministic request payload
- initial_latent(sample)       -> the shared starting noise as a numpy array, or
                                  None for non-generative models (strict only)
- to_request(sample, latents)  -> (method, path, json_body) for the mstar server;
                                  embed `latents` (base64 .npy) when not None
- from_response(response)      -> the candidate output as a comparable artifact
                                  (video: an (T,H,W,C) uint8 numpy array; None if invalid)
- load()                       -> load the upstream reference model (strict only)
- oracle(sample, latents)      -> the reference output, same artifact type as
                                  from_response, denoising `latents` when provided

Weights are at /model (docker) or resolve from the HF id. Do NOT reuse the
candidate's mstar code here — the oracle must be the independent upstream model.
"""

